# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and host state out of it.
#
# `.env` in particular: the image must never carry credentials. Configuration arrives as
# environment variables at run time, which is also what lets the same image run in local,
# staging and production without a rebuild.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.github

# Host build state. Copying these in would shadow the image's own install.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# Docs and local-only tooling do not belong in a runtime image.
*.md
!README.md
docker-compose.yml
